To get a Klein bottle from a square:

 i) Take one pair of parallel edges and paste them together.

 ii) take the other two edges of the (now) cylinder, give them half
     a twist and join them together (you need to do the rotation in 4space).

Voila!

Some notes: this is EXACTLY analogous to a Moebius strip.
Its a 3D non-orientable
object (meaning it has no sides and one surface, no separate insides and out)
just as a Moebius strip is a 2D non-orientable object.
Incidently they're chiral - there are righties and lefties.
Moebius strips are also chiral - you can make the 1/2 twist cw or ccw.

